---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const specialities = ['dbt', 'BigQuery', 'Snowflake', 'Data Mesh', 'Data modelling', 'Training', 'Query optimisation', 'AI-assisted development'];
---
<Base title="About" description="Martina Zaccaron is an analytics engineer and dbt Labs technical instructor with 10+ years in data, helping teams get dbt right.">
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Hi, I'm Martina</h1>
  </div>
  <section style="padding-top:1rem">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="intro">
        <img class="portrait" src="/uploads/martina-portrait.png" alt="Martina Zaccaron" width="176" height="220" />
        <p class="lead-p">I'm an analytics engineer and dbt Labs technical instructor with 10+ years of experience working in data, based in Senigallia, Italy. I help data teams get dbt right: set up properly from day one, or fixed when the project has become slow, messy or fragile.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Recent work</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>dbt Labs:</strong> technical instructor.</li>
          <li><strong>Kering Group</strong> (via Lenstra): delivered 7+ production data products end to end on dbt and BigQuery, onboarded 10+ teams onto a shared enterprise platform, and maintained and improved existing data products.</li>
          <li><strong>Cleo:</strong> kept an existing dbt project moving and cut run time and CI check time by 50%. Reviewed critical transaction pipelines, helped build a dbt health monitoring dashboard, onboarded product analysts to dbt, and set up new models for the payments squad.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>My background is in mathematics, and I like turning messy problems into clear structures. I enjoy upskilling teams so good practices outlast my time on a project.</p>
        <p>I'm a foodie. That's where <em>Food for Data</em> comes from. The <a href="/blog/">blog</a> is where I share what I learn.</p>

        <h2>Specialities</h2>
        <ul class="tools">
          {specialities.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Need help with dbt? Let's talk</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
